    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:NorGrith">Nor Grið</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="473" ed="#liebermann"/>[cyric]frið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#NorGrith_2.lnote.oe.1"/> ⁊ s<hi rend="italic">anctu</hi>s Wilfriðus ⁊ s<hi rend="italic">anctu</hi>s</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" n="1[b]" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="32" ed="#rabin-doml"/>cyricfrið and sanctus Wilfriðus and sanctus</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="473" ed="#liebermann"/>[Fortsetzung von 1]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">[Continuation of clause 1; see line 1.]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-b"><pb n="33" ed="#rabin-doml"/>the compensation owed for a violation of Church sanctuary at Saint Peter’s, Saint Wilfrid’s,</ab>
        <note type="editorial">K: the line ends with ‘sanctus’ (the next line begins ‘[Iohann]es’); ‘Petrus’ had been repeated in error from line 1.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cyricfrið: reconstructed by Liebermann</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Saint Peter’s, Saint Wilfrid’s, and within the walls of Saint John’s: The three churches specified are those at York, Ripon, and Beverly. Saint John’s . . . compensated: “John’s,” “hundred,” and “cannot be compensated” are all reconstructed.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="NorGrith_2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">473</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Sievers Gramm.</hi> 198, 5 <hi rend="italic">A</hi>²</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gramm.</hi> 198, 5 A²</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="NorGrith_2.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">267</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl durch gemeinsames Benutzen von VIII Atr 4f. = I Cn 3f. stimmt dies z. T. wörtlich zu Northu 19. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably through common use of VIII Atr 4f. = I Cn 3f., this agrees in part word for word with Northu 19. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
